// Perceptual Grade 1.23.2 | Linear XYZ in/out, reference-white Y=1.
// Exposure + CAT16 + linear 3x3 -> modCAM16-UCS -> tone remap -> driver contributions -> XYZ.
// 52 tonal values + 3 global contributions. 62 float sliders, 13 int sliders,
// 1 whole-nit value box and 5 dropdowns. No RPCC, hue masks or web dependency.
// J_HK=sqrt(J_A^2+66*C), dark surround, D=1, eccentricity -.1475*sin(h).
// Reference/background defaults 203/20.3 nits. Hard black plateau; no toe smoothing.
// Additive J; bounded tonal hue concentration, scalar hue rotation and positive scalar log-radius gain; weighted Adaptance last.
// Complementary p=2 drivers: s=75*C/J_A, midpoint s=35, neutral fade C^2/(C^2+4).
// Input levels: neutral nits. All chroma gains: log2 stops.
// Driver labels: C_l=lower-saturation response; C_h=higher-saturation response. Output C=chroma. Canonical UI edition.
// Stage 2 preserves modCAM16 saturation C/J_A and hue while remapping J_HK.
// Exact reset bypass. H-K repair preserves hue, caps H lift at 20%, and reduces C.
// Fourth-root achromatic energy; fixed global engineering constants.
// No inverse round-trip accuracy test. Necessary domain/finite guards remain.
// Remaining inverse-domain failures fall back to stage 2, then stage-1 XYZ.
// Curves are analytic. No sampled value table or Quintic-2048 interpolation.
